hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1166","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told him that he asked Aisha: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Ramadan? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray more than eleven rak’ahs in Ramadan or at any other time, so do not forget about it. Their beauty and length, then he prays four, so do not ask about their beauty and length, then he prays three. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, should you pray? Before you get stressed? He said: “O Aisha, my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep.”"
